# The network of "A tunnel to the cloud": the shop's office, its VPN
# gateway, the internet, and a cloud provider's VPN gateway with the shop's
# new cloud network behind it.
#
#   office --- vpn ==(internet)== cloud --[vpc]-- app
#   192.168.10.10  198.51.100.10   203.0.113.10    10.30.1.10
#
# vpn is the office's VPN gateway, the learner's, built from nothing.
# cloud stands in for a cloud provider's VPN gateway (AS 64600, a private
# AS number) and isn't the learner's: its tunnel interface, its IPsec
# connection and its BGP are scenery.
machine office
machine vpn router
machine internet router
machine cloud router
machine app

link office:eth0=192.168.10.10/24 vpn:lan=192.168.10.1/24
link vpn:wan=198.51.100.10/24 internet:vpn=198.51.100.1/24
link internet:cloud=203.0.113.1/24 cloud:wan=203.0.113.10/24
lan vpc cloud:vpc=10.30.0.1/16 app:eth0=10.30.1.10/16
route office default via 192.168.10.1
route app default via 10.30.0.1

# The provider's end of the tunnel. Key 9 is the mark that ties its vti0 to
# the IPsec SA whose mark_in and mark_out are 9 (cloud's swanctl file).
tunnel cloud vti0 vti local 203.0.113.10 remote 198.51.100.10 key 9 addr 169.254.44.1/30

run vpn frr strongswan
run cloud frr strongswan
run app nginx
